 "summaries": [
  {
   "version": "Introduced in House",
   "date": "2019-06-26",
   "text": "Protecting People From Surprise Medical Bills Act\n This bill makes a series of changes relating to health care costs and billing practices.\n Among other things, the bill\n applies in-network cost-sharing requirements to certain emergency and related non-emergency services that are provided out-of-network;\n requires health insurers to include in-network and out-of-network deductibles, as well as out-of-pocket maximum limitations, on enrollee insurance cards;\n requires health insurers to provide online and print directories of in-network health care providers; and\n prohibits health care providers from billing individuals for services more than a year after such services are provided."
  }
 ],
